{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-8939-1",
  "summary": "libxtst vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain RECORD\nreplies from the X server. A malicious X server could possibly use this\nissue to cause libXtst clients to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-94286)\n\nTobias Stoeckmann discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain\nmemory operations. A malicious X server could possibly use this issue to\ncause libXtst to access memory out of bounds, resulting in a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-7951)\n\nTobias Stoeckmann discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain\nreplies from the X server. A malicious X server could possibly use this\nissue to cause libXtst to enter an infinite loop, resulting in a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-7952)",
